                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net @vernon.mauery@gmail.com could you check on this PR."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Ed has concerns, removing my +1."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "@spinler@us.ibm.com\nThanks for letting me know. Could you please share Ed\u2019s specific concerns so I can address them?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_probe.cpp",
                    "line": 235,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not a huge fan of using regex here.  std::regex is insanely slow, we're making a string copy to use it;  We don't really expect anything other than space here, so I suspect we can just check for that?\n\nThis fix also looks incorrect for things that aren't conjunctions.  \"FALSE\" is a complete statement, and doesn't require a word boundary.\n\nLong term, I would like to see a real parser integrated, like:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/36517 so that we're operating on an AST and tokens, not string parsing.\n\nShort term, would simply changing the regex match for \"AND\" and \"OR\" to \" AND \" and \" OR \" fix this without needing regex, while still keeping the unary functions working?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_probe.cpp",
                    "line": 235,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "To fix this kind of issues added the logic:\nFor instance: probe = xyz.openbmc_project.UsbDevice({'VENDOR_ID': '2frrr3'}) would fail to be probed and would be considered as a conjunction statement - since it has OR at 36th index (in vendOR_id)\nNote: please Suggest the any testcases want to test."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_probe.cpp",
                    "line": 235,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net\ncould you please share your specific concerns so I can address them?"
                }
